# Khyata System

A backend system built using ASP.NET Core and Clean Architecture.  
The project is designed to support both main application APIs and a dedicated admin API with a scalable and maintainable structure.

---

# Tech Stack

- ASP.NET Core Web API
- Clean Architecture
- Entity Framework Core
- SQL Server
- JWT Authentication
- AutoMapper
- Dependency Injection

---

# Project Structure

Khyata
│
├── Khyata.API              Main application API
├── Khyata.Admin            Admin API
├── Khyata.Application      Business logic layer
├── Khyata.Domain           Domain entities and enums
├── Khyata.Infrastructure   Data access and repositories
└── Khyata.sln              Solution file

---

# Architecture

The system follows Clean Architecture principles:

- Domain Layer: Core business entities and rules
- Application Layer: Business logic and services
- Infrastructure Layer: Database and external services
- API Layer: Controllers and endpoints

---

# Features

- JWT Authentication and Authorization
- Role-based access control (Admin / User)
- Customer management
- Order management
- Workspace management
- Separation of concerns
- Scalable architecture

---

# Run Locally

## Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/Khyata.git

---

## Restore dependencies

dotnet restore

---

## Update database

dotnet ef database update

---

## Run main API

dotnet run --project Khyata.API

---

## Run admin API

dotnet run --project Khyata.Admin

---

# Configuration

Update appsettings.json:

{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "DefaultConnection": "Server=.;Database=KhyataDB;Trusted_Connection=True;"
  },
  "Jwt": {
    "Key": "your-secret-key",
    "Issuer": "Khyata",
    "Audience": "KhyataUsers"
  }
}

---

# Notes

- Admin API is separated for security and management purposes.
- Shared logic is located in Application, Domain, and Infrastructure layers.
- Both APIs depend on the same core architecture.

